# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MEDIA GUARD — added 2026-11-13
# Rule: Git holds knowledge. Media lives outside and gets one index line.
# Source of truth: config/media-policy.json
# Enforced by: scripts/media-check.mjs  +  .github/workflows/repo-guard.yml
#
# Why a whole section and not one line: the old rule was `deliverables/*.mp4`,
# which matched one directory and nothing else. 185 media files (1.1 GB) had
# already got through. Patterns below are anchored with ** so a file three
# folders deep is caught the same as a file in the root.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# video
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm
*.mkv
*.m4v
*.enc

# audio
*.wav
*.mp3
*.flac
*.m4a
*.aac
*.opus
*.aiff

# image plates / heavy lossless
*.psd
*.exr
*.hdr
*.tif
*.tiff
*.ai
*.sketch

# 3d
*.blend
*.blend1
*.glb
*.gltf
*.fbx
*.obj
*.usd
*.usdz

# archives and bundles
*.zip
*.7z
*.bundle
*.iso
*.dmg


# --- working folders that hold media but are not media -------------------
# NOTE: must stay root-anchored. A bare 'references/' also swallows
# skills/*/references/ — 1,149 files of documented skill material (*.md, *.js)
# that are knowledge, not media.
/references/
refs/**/*.enc
google_drive/
image-search/
gpu-engine/keyframes/
gpu-engine/clips/
production/extinct-life/*/keyframes/
production/extinct-life/*/renders/
production/extinct-life/*/frames/
production/extinct-life/*/output/
production/extinct-life/*/working/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXCEPTIONS — must be the LAST thing in this file. Git applies the last
# matching pattern, so a negation placed above *.mp4 is dead code. Measured:
# the approved proof master was being ignored by line 68 (*.mp4) even though
# it sits on config/media-policy.json keep_in_git.paths.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!public/thumbnails/**
!public/proof/**
!public/showreel/**
!public/demo-poster.jpg
# The showreel the portfolio plays (25 MB) is load-bearing product surface, not
# a deliverable: src/B2BStudio.jsx renders <video src="/demo-preview.mp4">.
# Without this line it is tracked-but-ignored, which is a trap — the moment
# anybody releases it with `git rm --cached` (exactly what this migration does
# to every other video), render-showreel-60fps.yml's `git add public/demo-preview.mp4`
# starts exiting 1 and that pipeline dies. Naming it here closes that door.
!public/demo-preview.mp4
!deliverables/MON-DEMO26_Proof_Over_Promises_v3_1080p60_Master.mp4
!docs/research/**/*.csv.gz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RENDER EVIDENCE — the bulk of the remaining tracked bytes.
# Measured 2026-11-13: 560 of 771 tracked images (176 MB) are frame extracts
# from films that already have a released master. The text evidence stays:
#   EVIDENCE.json, QC.json, *.csv, *.md, *.py  -> all still tracked
# The JPGs are a rendering of numbers already stored as text.
# Rule for a scripted extraction folder: generator + pinned sha256 must exist
# in config/media-policy.json -> regenerable_evidence.
# Workflow-produced stills (film-*/inspection/) are output, not evidence.
#
# WHY THESE ARE MEDIA GLOBS AND NOT BARE FOLDER RULES (fixed 2026-11-13):
# they used to read `production/extinct-life/film-*/inspection/`, which ignored
# the WHOLE folder. That folder also holds the QC text — motion-QC.json,
# render-<a>-<b>.json — which is the actual evidence, and the header two lines
# up says text evidence stays. Two things broke because of it:
#   1. `git add production/.../inspection` exits 1 on an ignored path, and
#      GitHub Actions runs steps with `bash -e`, so extinct-v8-premium.yml
#      failed the job outright (run 43340437009, step "Preserve original
#      production inspection"). Re-adding a bare `!` negation does NOT help:
#      git never re-includes files under an excluded directory.
#   2. Every new QC json would have been silently dropped from the repo.
# Ignoring the extensions instead keeps the stills out and the numbers in.
# `git add <folder>` on a folder with ignored children is legal and exits 0.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
production/extinct-life/film-*/inspection/**
# Frame extracts are measurement output. Measured 2026-11-13: 537 .jpg / 142 MB
# were tracked across nine folders, all regenerable from a master pinned by
# sha256 in config/media-policy.json -> regenerable_evidence. Released to Drive
# (two archives, hashes verified) and ignored from here on so they cannot
# regrow. Scoped to .jpg only: the .png files under production/ are SOURCE
# assets (scene plates, thumbnails, textures) and are load-bearing, not stills.
production/**/*.jpg
production/extinct-life/film-*/encoded-inspection/**
production/extinct-life/review-v*/full-resolution/**
production/extinct-life/review-v*/seconds/**
production/extinct-life/review-v*/motion/**
production/extinct-life/longform-mammoth/**/inspection/**
production/extinct-life/longform-mammoth/**/stills/**
production/extinct-life/homotherium-short/inspection/**
gpu-engine/keyframes/**

# ...but keep the measurement text inside those folders. Last-match-wins, so
# these must sit BELOW the rules above; they are scoped to the folders named
# above and cannot re-admit media anywhere else in the repo.
!production/extinct-life/**/inspection/**/*.json
!production/extinct-life/**/inspection/**/*.csv
!production/extinct-life/**/inspection/**/*.md
!production/extinct-life/**/inspection/**/*.txt
!production/extinct-life/**/seconds/**/*.json
!production/extinct-life/**/seconds/**/*.csv
!production/extinct-life/**/motion/**/*.json
!production/extinct-life/**/motion/**/*.csv
!production/extinct-life/**/full-resolution/**/*.json
!production/extinct-life/**/full-resolution/**/*.csv
!gpu-engine/keyframes/**/*.json
